## Review section: Bounded independent review & behavior-preserving remediation

> **Triggered by:** all implementation sections green.
> **Policy:** `references/adversarial-review.md` and `references/implementation-review.md`
> **Goal:** one bounded `RV-*` cycle over the whole change. Required for implement approval.
> **Cycle:** `implement-N`
> Use the current manifest review epoch.

- [ ] Launch a **fresh auditor subagent** for one broad pass. Always cover structure/ownership, applicable language idioms, and tests/behavior preservation; add runtime/security/operational lenses when scope evidence makes them relevant. No mandatory N/A boilerplate.
- [ ] Consolidate one complete blocker/major batch. Record each original finding below and attest with `review-log.mjs`; do not issue later batches.
- [ ] Apply one behavior-preserving remediation for the complete batch (or record an evidence-based clean rationale). Firm-seam tests stay green; a firm-seam failure is a kickback, not a test edit.
- [ ] Run the full test suite — must be green after remediation.
- [ ] Launch a **distinct fresh verifier subagent** to check only original RV IDs; no broad rediscovery or new low/major findings. A remediation-caused blocker regression may be recorded through `--regression`; at most one targeted correction/reverification closes it through `--regression-resolution`.
- [ ] Record structured auditor and verifier attestations under the current `implement-N` epoch; verifier resolutions reference every original RV ID.
- [ ] User approves → implement approval → approved (blocked until the verifier approval is recorded)

